; Freelancer Decomp: a reimplementation of the Freelancer (2003) game client and engine,
; faithful to the behaviour of the original game.
; This file was reconstructed by reverse engineering the binaries of Freelancer 1.1,
; developed by Digital Anvil.
; Author: Giperion.

; FLServer.exe export surface = retail's (dumpbin -exports EXE\FLServer.exe: 71 names,
; ordinals 1..71). Retail compiled its own copies of these shared-header class members into the
; exe because the headers resolved to dllexport in its build; every copy is instruction-identical
; to the owner DLL's own export. Our headers resolve to dllimport in FLServer, so each one is
; forwarded to the owner DLL's export of the same name (checked against dumpbin -exports of
; bin\Server.dll, bin\DALib.dll, bin\Common.dll). Exceptions:
;   @45 GetMOTD: the modern wchar_t decoration (_W) replaces VC6's G (accepted: compare by
;       class/method/arity, AGENTS.md); retail ?GetMOTD@PlayerDB@@QAEAAV?$basic_string@GU?$char_traits@G@std@@V?$allocator@G@2@@std@@XZ
;   @57 ServerLogf: FLServer's own function (.text:0040e330), exported from the local definition;
;       its declaration must mangle to ?ServerLogf@@YAHUErrorCode@@PBDZZ.
; The ??_7 vftables are data in retail; forwarders carry no DATA attribute.
NAME FLServer
